WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.030
Night.

2
00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:04.310
A dark garden, one candle burning.

3
00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.320
A man walks alone.

4
00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:10.130
On one side, a glowing label: my friend.

5
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:15.280
On the other, a small egg, its
shadow stretched long by the candle.

6
00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.000
He says it aloud: "It
must be by his death".

7
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:21.520
Yet he admits no personal cause.

8
00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:24.250
So how does he talk himself into it?

9
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.440
In this mission, you'll
meet a man who loves Caesar,

10
00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.180
yet fears the people will make him king.

11
00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:35.190
You'll take apart his orchard soliloquy,
as he reasons with himself, alone.

12
00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:38.820
And you'll crack open one
image: a serpent's egg,

13
00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:41.890
and the order to "kill him in the shell".

14
00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.550
Your mission: explain how Brutus
talks himself into killing his friend.
